1
00:00:00,450 --> 00:00:04,154
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.

2
00:00:04,154 --> 00:00:08,407
Let any agent shop for you, only within the limits you set.

3
00:00:09,133 --> 00:00:11,071
AI agents can now shop for us.

4
00:00:11,071 --> 00:00:13,876
But to pay, we hand them a card with no limits.

5
00:00:13,876 --> 00:00:15,304
One injected prompt,

6
00:00:15,304 --> 00:00:18,359
and real money moves before anyone approves it.

7
00:00:18,817 --> 00:00:21,910
PACT sits between any AI agent and PayPal.

8
00:00:21,910 --> 00:00:23,643
Agents can only ask.

9
00:00:23,643 --> 00:00:26,674
A deterministic policy engine authorizes,

10
00:00:26,674 --> 00:00:29,771
a human approves, and PayPal executes.

11
00:00:30,133 --> 00:00:32,333
It starts with a spending mandate.

12
00:00:32,333 --> 00:00:35,162
This one allows electronics from one merchant,

13
00:00:35,162 --> 00:00:37,088
up to $100 per purchase.

14
00:00:37,449 --> 00:00:40,617
First, the built-in reference agent is asked

15
00:00:40,617 --> 00:00:42,993
for a keyboard that costs $125.

16
00:00:42,993 --> 00:00:45,010
Gemini recommends it.

17
00:00:45,365 --> 00:00:48,512
Blocked. Attempted $125. Allowed $100.

18
00:00:48,512 --> 00:00:51,453
No approve button, no PayPal order.

19
00:00:51,453 --> 00:00:54,644
The AI cannot override the mandate.

20
00:00:54,982 --> 00:00:58,550
Next, an $89 keyboard passes all ten rules.

21
00:00:58,550 --> 00:01:02,158
But passing policy is not authorization.

22
00:01:02,498 --> 00:01:04,113
I review the budget impact

23
00:01:04,113 --> 00:01:06,012
and approve this exact purchase.

24
00:01:06,012 --> 00:01:08,589
My approval is sealed with a fingerprint.

25
00:01:08,948 --> 00:01:12,279
A SHA-256 hash of the product, merchant, price,

26
00:01:12,279 --> 00:01:15,490
quantity, mandate rules and requesting agent.

27
00:01:15,490 --> 00:01:17,731
A forged approval is refused,

28
00:01:17,731 --> 00:01:21,797
and the hash is checked again before every PayPal step.

29
00:01:22,131 --> 00:01:24,687
PACT creates a real PayPal Sandbox order,

30
00:01:24,687 --> 00:01:27,702
and the buyer approves it in PayPal Checkout.

31
00:01:28,048 --> 00:01:30,568
Back in PACT, the server asks PayPal directly

32
00:01:30,568 --> 00:01:32,232
whether the buyer approved.

33
00:01:32,232 --> 00:01:34,669
Only then can the payment be captured.

34
00:01:35,031 --> 00:01:36,279
Captured.

35
00:01:36,279 --> 00:01:40,020
A real PayPal capture ID, status COMPLETED,

36
00:01:40,020 --> 00:01:42,031
for exactly $89.

37
00:01:42,381 --> 00:01:44,827
What if something changes after approval?

38
00:01:44,827 --> 00:01:46,624
I approve a second keyboard.

39
00:01:46,624 --> 00:01:49,020
Then the merchant raises the price.

40
00:01:49,365 --> 00:01:51,330
The approval is void at once.

41
00:01:51,330 --> 00:01:54,768
A change can never silently inherit an old approval.

42
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:57,856
Connecting an outside agent takes seconds.

43
00:01:57,856 --> 00:02:00,269
It gets one mandate and its own key,

44
00:02:00,269 --> 00:02:02,986
shown once and stored only as a hash.

45
00:02:03,331 --> 00:02:06,357
Claude, ChatGPT or your own agent

46
00:02:06,357 --> 00:02:09,088
use PACT's API or MCP server.

47
00:02:09,088 --> 00:02:11,450
Told money is no object,

48
00:02:11,450 --> 00:02:14,800
this Gemini agent still gets a no.

49
00:02:15,147 --> 00:02:17,381
In-policy requests wait for you,

50
00:02:17,381 --> 00:02:20,061
and every step lands in the audit trail.

51
00:02:20,061 --> 00:02:22,600
Agents can ask. Only you approve.

52
00:02:22,963 --> 00:02:25,356
And PACT isn't tied to one catalog.

53
00:02:25,356 --> 00:02:27,581
A Shopify-format store syncs in,

54
00:02:27,581 --> 00:02:29,973
and its offers face the same rules.

55
00:02:29,973 --> 00:02:34,117
This cable is blocked, because that store isn't on my mandate.

56
00:02:34,480 --> 00:02:38,001
Any platform plugs in with one connector that returns offers.

57
00:02:38,001 --> 00:02:40,145
The policy engine, the fingerprint

58
00:02:40,145 --> 00:02:42,487
and the PayPal flow never change.

59
00:02:42,930 --> 00:02:46,376
Agents request. The policy engine authorizes.

60
00:02:46,376 --> 00:02:49,106
A human approves. PayPal executes.

61
00:02:49,106 --> 00:02:53,387
PACT. The payment authorization gateway for AI agents.
